## 7. Gated self-improvement

### 7.1 The loop

Four modules (ppe/monitor.py, ppe/diagnose.py, ppe/improve.py, ppe/verify.py) run under one orchestrator (ppe/loop.py) with a state file.

- **Monitor.** The confidence-drift estimator of section 6, refitted on validation cells with the scenario conditions left out. Its alarm
  threshold is the 99th percentile of the estimate over clean validation windows: {{shift/val/clean/all/monitor_alarm_threshold|.4f}}.
- **Diagnose.** Four label-free image-health checks per frame (black, flat or covered, frozen, blur) map a finding to the brief's three responses:
  camera fault (alert a human, do not retrain), temporal drop (log and wait) and persistent shift ({{cfg:3:configs/loop/p5_site_shift.yaml}} consecutive alarmed windows; enter improve).
- **Improve.** Buffer {{shift/train/stream/all/frames_pooled|int}} frames after the shift is declared, mine the {{shift/train/stream/all/frames_mined|int}} with the highest augmentation disagreement,
  pseudo-label them, write a {{shift/train/stream/all/human_minutes|n}}-frame sample for human checking, and fine-tune from the current weights with {{shift/train/stream/all/replay_frames|int}} clean replay images
  (10 epochs, backbone frozen).
- **Verify.** The brief's gate on the frozen golden set: every no_* recall not lower than the incumbent's, mAP@0.5 not lower by more than
  {{promo:site_shift/map50_tolerance|.2f}} (fixed in the configuration before the run), and recall on the new-site sample improved. Every decision is written to results/promotions.csv; the last three promoted weights are kept for rollback.

What the scenarios are not: the streams are 40-frame windows of **training** images under the Phase 2 corruptions or synthetic camera faults, and
the new-site sample is the validation split under the same corruption. The pseudo-labels are the images' own labels, a perfect-teacher stand-in.
[FLAG: No real teacher was used. YOLO-World pseudo-labels (configs/loop/p5_site_shift_yolo_world.yaml) could not run because its text-encoder weights were unreachable, so the pseudo-label error rate of a real teacher is missing; the logged rate of {{shift/train/stream/all/pseudo_label_error_rate_vs_source}} holds by construction.]
[FLAG: Human verification has not happened: human minutes are {{shift/train/stream/all/human_minutes|int}} and the human pseudo-label error rate is "pending" in promotions.csv. The paper cannot report the human cost of the loop, and must not describe it as self-improving without human input.]
[FLAG: No scenario uses a real site stream; the "site shift" is low light applied to training images the detector has already seen clean.]

